-- title:
--   Supersingular descended model for q=3: affine chart and nodes
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`; for an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, write $\mathcal{O}_0 := A\cap k_0$ for `A.comap (algebraMap ↥k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))`, the valuation subring of $k_0$ of elements whose image lies in $A$.
--
--   **Level and residual data.** A prime $q$ with $q = 3$; a natural number $M' \neq 0$ with $q \nmid M'$; a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$ (a rigidity guard on the auxiliary level). A valuation subring $A \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; its residue field is written $\kappa =$ `ResidueField A`. A finite set $W$ of places of $\kappa$ in `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` $= \kappa(j_q, j_q(q^{M'}\text{-expansion}))$, namely the intermediate field of $\kappa((q))$ generated over $\kappa$ by `jqModC κ` and `jqNModC κ M'`; the hypothesis `hW` says that $W$ consists exactly of the members of `ssPlaces q M' κ`, that is, of the places $w$ that are rational (the structure map $\kappa \to w.\mathrm{ResidueField}$ is surjective), satisfy `IsAffineGeomPlace κ M'`, and whose value $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ on the generator `jGeomGen κ M'` lies in `ssJSet q κ`; $s$ is a chosen element of $W$.
--
--   **The two function fields and the constant reduction.** The hypothesis `hle` asserts the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` $\le$ `fieldBar q M'` of intermediate fields of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$: the first is the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the full level-$M'$ modular function field `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` (the field generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the $d$-fold $q$-expansions of $j_q$ for $d \mid M'$), the second the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$, $H =$ `levelH q M'` the kernel of $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$. Further data: a `ConstantReduction` $R_0$ of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`, i.e. a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ of the former whose contraction to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is $A$, a surjective ring map $R_0.\mathrm{residue}$ onto the latter with kernel the maximal ideal, a map on places of degree- and order-compatible type, and compatibility of $R_0.\mathrm{residue}$ with $A \to \kappa$ on constants. The hypothesis `hR₀` says that this reduction is computed coefficientwise: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   **Small-field data.** An intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ with $\pi_0 \in A$, subject to: $\mathcal{O}_0$ is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), is a henselian local ring (`hhens`), and has algebraically closed residue field (`hres`); and `hκ`, that every $a \in A$ differs from some element $c$ of $\mathcal{O}_0$ by an element of the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   **Auxiliary constants.** A prime $\ell$ with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \neq q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; an element $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lying in $A$ and satisfying $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   **Base layer.** An intermediate field $K_b$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/k_0$ with $K_b = \bot$ (so $K_b = k_0$); a valuation subring $A_b$ of $K_b$ whose elements are exactly those with image in $A$; an element $\varpi_b \neq 0$ of $A_b$ generating its maximal ideal.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Give `fieldBar q M'` its $k_0$-algebra structure through $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Then for every intermediate field $F_0$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ which is the level field, i.e. such that $f \in F_0$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient $f_n$ ($n \in \mathbb{Z}$) lies in the image of $k_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, there exists a valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ with the following properties.
--
--   (1) $W_0 \cap k_0 = \mathcal{O}_0$: for $x \in k_0$, $x \in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$.
--
--   (2) $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring.
--
--   (3) The image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (4) $W_0$ lies over $s$: for every $g \in$ `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose coefficientwise image in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and which is regular wherever $j_q$ is (for every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(j_q)$ implies $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(g)$), if the $R_0$-residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$, then the image of $g$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$, and for every $c \in k_0 \cap A$ whose residue in $\kappa$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference (image of $g$) $- c$ lies in $W_0$ and in its maximal ideal.
--
--   (5) Level stability: for every $\zeta \in$ `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M') \subseteq \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, and every $f \in$ `fieldBar q M'` with both $f$ and `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ f` in $F_0$, one has $f \in W_0$ if and only if `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ f` $\in W_0$.
--
--   (6) There exist a subring $B$ of `fieldBar q M'` and an $A_b$-algebra structure on $B$ such that:
--
--   (6a) the structure map $A_b \to B$ is the inclusion $A_b \subseteq K_b \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to$ `fieldBar q M'`;
--
--   (6b) $B$ is contained in the join (as intermediate fields over $k_0$) of $F_0$ with the subfield generated over $k_0$ by the image of $K_b$;
--
--   (6c) every element of that join is of the form $g/h$ with $g, h \in B$, $h \neq 0$;
--
--   (6d) $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$, and $B/(\varpi_b B)$ has Krull dimension at most $1$;
--
--   (6e) every $f \in B$ lies in $F_0$ and its image lies in $W_0$;
--
--   (6f) the image of $\varpi_b$ in $B$ is a prime element;
--
--   (6g) $W_0$ is the localisation of $B$ at that prime: $f \in F_0$ lies in $W_0$ if and only if $f\,h = g$ for some $g, h \in B$ with the image of $\varpi_b$ not dividing $h$;
--
--   (6h) the image of $j_q$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $B$;
--
--   (6i) $B$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` for every $\zeta \in$ `Idx q` and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$;
--
--   (6j) identification of the special fibre with a Drinfeld quotient: for every algebra structure of $\kappa$ over `GaloisField q 2`, every hypothesis that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) (the quotient of $\kappa[x_0,x_1]$ by the Drinfeld polynomial minus $1$) is a domain, and every $\zeta \in$ `Idx q`, there exist a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of `GaloisField q 2` and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ to [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) (the fixed field in the Drinfeld function field of the subgroup generated by the action of $C_s$) such that: the cardinality of $C_s$ equals $2\,\cdot$ `placeWidthChar q M' s`, the latter being `jWidthChar q` of $s.\mathrm{evalAt}($`jGeomGen`$)$ divided by `placeRamificationJ M' s` (for $q = 3$ the numerator is $6$ at $j = 0$ and $1$ otherwise); the kernel of $\rho$ is the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi_b$; $\rho$ on $A_b$ is the reduction $A_b \to \kappa$ followed by the structure map of the Drinfeld quotient field; every element of the Drinfeld quotient field is of the form $\rho(g)/\rho(h)$ with $g, h \in B$ and $\rho(h) \neq 0$; an element of the quotient field lies in the range of $\rho$ exactly when its image in the Drinfeld function field lies in the image of the coordinate ring; and $\rho$ intertwines the level automorphisms with the Drinfeld $H$-action: for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ such that $(\mathrm{red}_q(\gamma), 1)$ lies in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276), and $f \in B$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹ f` $\in B$, the image of $\rho$ on the latter equals `hFunctionFieldAction` at $(\mathrm{red}_q(\gamma), 1)$ applied to $\rho(f)$;
--
--   (6k) the $q+1$ nodes: there exists a finite set `nodes` of subrings of $F_0$ with $\#$`nodes` $= q+1$ such that:
--
--   (i) the level automorphisms permute the nodes: for every $\zeta$, every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every $O \in$ `nodes` there is $O' \in$ `nodes` with $f \in O \iff$ `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ f` $\in O'$, for all $f$ such that both lie in $F_0$;
--
--   (ii) the action is transitive: for every $\zeta$ and all $O, O' \in$ `nodes` there is $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ realising $O \mapsto O'$ in the sense of (i);
--
--   (iii) the nodes are pairwise distinguished: for $O \neq O'$ in `nodes` there is $f \in F_0$ belonging to both which is a non-unit of $O$ and a unit of $O'$;
--
--   (iv) covering: every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ satisfying the analogues of (1) and (4) with $V$ in place of $W_0$ either contains $B$ (every $f \in B$ lies in $F_0$ with image in $V$) or dominates a node, i.e. there is $O \in$ `nodes` with $O \subseteq V$ and with every non-unit of $O$ lying in the maximal ideal of $V$;
--
--   (v) for each $O \in$ `nodes`: $O \subseteq W_0$; $O$ is a local noetherian ring; $O \cap k_0 = \mathcal{O}_0$ in the sense of (1); every $f \in O$ is congruent to a constant, i.e. there is $x \in k_0 \cap A$ with image in $O$ such that $f - x$ is not a unit of $O$. Moreover there exist a natural number $E_0 \ge 1$ together with a unit $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_0$ (both $v$ and $v^{-1}$ in $A$) satisfying $\pi_0^{E_0} = \varpi_t^{\,2\,\cdot\,\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s}\, v$, a proof that the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $O$, elements $c_x, c_y \in O$, a unit $u$ of $O$, a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the adic completion of $O$ at its maximal ideal onto `UVCrossingModel` of the adic completion $\widehat{\mathcal{O}_0}$ with parameter $\pi_0^{E_0}$ — that is, $\widehat{\mathcal{O}_0}[[U,V]]/(UV - \pi_0^{E_0})$ — and units $\gamma_U, \gamma_V$ of that crossing model, such that:
--
--   $c_x c_y = \pi_0^{E_0} u$ in $O$; $\iota$ carries the image of each $x \in k_0 \cap A$ lying in $O$ to the corresponding constant of the crossing model; $\iota(c_x) = \gamma_U \cdot U$ and $\iota(c_y) = \gamma_V \cdot V$; $c_y$ lies in $W_0$ and in the maximal ideal of $W_0$, while $c_x$, whenever it lies in $W_0$, lies outside the maximal ideal;
--
--   and there exists a valuation subring $W_x$ of $F_0$ (the second branch through the node) with: $O \subseteq W_x$; $W_x \cap k_0 = \mathcal{O}_0$ in the sense of (1); $W_x$ is a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $\pi_0$; an element $t \in W_x$ whose residue is transcendental in the sense that for every polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ all of whose coefficients lie in $A$, if $p(t)$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ then the image of every coefficient of $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$; $c_x$, whenever it lies in $W_x$, lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$, and $c_y$, whenever it lies in $W_x$, does not; and, for every $g \in$ `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` with $R_0$-integral image and regular wherever $j_q$ is (as in (4)), the image of $g$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_x$, it lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ if and only if its $R_0$-residue vanishes, and if that residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$ then the image of $g$ lies in $O$ and, for every $c \in k_0 \cap A$ with image in $O$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference (image of $g$) $- c$ is a non-unit of $O$;
--
--   and there exists a subring $B_x$ of $F_0$ with: every $f \in B_x$ lies in $B$ and in $O$; every $f \in B_x$ is regular wherever the image of $j_q$ is, for places of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; $O$ is the localisation of $B_x$ at its non-units, i.e. $f \in O$ if and only if $f h = g$ for some $g, h \in B_x$ with $h$ a unit of $O$ whenever $h \in O$; $B_x$ has fraction field $F_0$, i.e. every $f \in F_0$ is $g/h$ with $g, h \in B_x$, $h \neq 0$; and $B_x$ is the subring generated by the image of $k_0 \cap A$ together with a finite set $T$ of elements of $F_0$.
--
--   This is the $q = 3$ instance, under the rigidity guard provided by an auxiliary prime $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$, of the construction of the semistable model of the full-level modular curve over the level field $F_0$ in a neighbourhood of a supersingular point: a discrete valuation ring $W_0$ lying over the chosen supersingular place $s$, a formally smooth finitely presented affine chart $B$ over the base $A_b$ whose special fibre is identified with a Drinfeld quotient curve, and the $q+1$ local rings of the nodes of that fibre, permuted transitively by the level automorphisms. It is obtained from the single comprehensive statement assembling chart, poles, moduli Hasse invariant, common chart, nodes, Igusa separation and inertia, and feeds the downstream statement retaining only the chart and the supersingular valuation ring as well as the statement comparing a subalgebra with the Drinfeld coordinate ring up to localisation.
